    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm stuck on my lit review. if i have a source with like 5 authors, how am i supposed to do the in-text citation for APA 7th vs chicago? i keep getting them mixed up.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For APA 7th edition, cite the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" in both in-text citations and the reference list. Chicago style typically requires listing all authors the first time they are cited, using \"et al.\" only if there are more than a certain number. When in doubt, check your instructor's specific guidelines, as requirements can vary even within each style.",
