      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In Chicago style, the treatment often depends on whether you are using Notes & Bibliography or Author-Date. For Notes & Bibliography, you usually use a shortened citation in subsequent footnotes. In Author-Date style, you generally list the full names the first time, but subsequent citations might vary slightly depending on the edition you are using. Always double-check your required style guide for consistency within your paper.",
